They also learned that to reach South Africa , they needed to go far out in the ocean , head for Brazil , and around 30 ° S go east again . Following the African coast southbound means upwind in the Southern hemisphere . In the Pacific ocean , the full wind circulation , which included both the trade wind easterlies and higher - latitude Westerlies , was unknown to Europeans until Andres de Urdaneta 's voyage in 1565 . The captain of a sailing ship seeks a course along which the winds can be expected to blow in the direction of travel . During the Age of Sail , the pattern of prevailing winds made various points of the globe easy or difficult to access , and therefore had a direct effect on European empire - building and thus on modern political geography . For example , Manila galleons could not sail into the wind at all . By the 18th century the importance of the trade winds to England 's merchant fleet for crossing the Atlantic Ocean had led both the general public and etymologists to identify the name with a later meaning of ' trade ' , `` ( foreign ) commerce '' .","entities":["Trade winds","Age of sail","African coast","wind circulation","trade wind easterlies","Westerlies","Andres de Urdaneta","prevailing winds","European empire-building","modern political geography","Manila galleons","England's merchant fleet","foreign commerce","voyage","England"],"facts":["Trade winds -LOCATED_IN-> Earth's equator","Trade winds -LOCATED_IN-> Earth's atmosphere","Trade winds -LOCATED_IN-> Troposphere","Trade winds -RELATED_TO-> Northern Hemisphere","Trade winds -LOCATED_IN-> the tropics"]}
