[E335b10] {"title":"Alice in Wonderland (1951 film)","text":"Alice in Wonderland (1951 film)
However , the composition was kept and the lyrics were changed . It later became the title song for Peter Pan ( which was in production at the same time ) , `` The Second Star to the Right '' . The title song , composed by Sammy Fain , has become a jazz standard , first adopted by jazz pianist Dave Brubeck ; featured first in 1952 , then on his 1957 Columbia album Dave Digs Disney . Izumi Yukimura sang her own theme song for the Japanese release of the film . The song , `` In a World of My Own , '' is included on the orange disc of Classic Disney : 60 Years of Musical Magic . Release and reception ( edit ) At the time , these creative decisions were met with great criticism from Carroll fans , as well as from British film and literary critics who accused Disney of `` Americanizing '' a great work of English literature .","entities":["jazz standard","The Second Star to the Right","Dave Brubeck","Dave Digs Disney","Izumi Yukimura","In a World of My Own","Classic Disney: 60 Years of Musical Magic","Alice in Wonderland (1951 film)","Peter Pan","Columbia","Disney","Sammy Fain"],"facts":["In a World of My Own -RELATED_TO-> Alice","Beyond the Laughing Sky -RELATED_TO-> In a World of My Own","Alice in Wonderland -RELATED_TO-> jazz standard","Beyond the Laughing Sky -RELATED_TO-> The Second Star to the Right","In a World of My Own -PART_OF-> Alice in Wonderland"]}
