In 2003 , they won the NFC first seed , but Westbrook went down in Week 17 , culminating in a loss to the Carolina Panthers in their 3rd straight NFC Championship . 2004 season and Super Bowl XXXIX In 2004 , the Philadelphia Eagles had their best season since 1960 , going 13 -- 1 before resting their starters and losing their next 2 , clinching the 1st seed for the second year in a row . McNabb set career highs , completing 64 % of his passes for 3,875 yards , though he did n't play all 16 games . McNabb became the first quarterback ever to throw more than 30 touchdowns and fewer than 10 interceptions in a season . His success could be attributed to the fact that he had a reliable receiver , Terrell Owens , who got 1,200 yards and 14 touchdowns in 14 games . After beating the Vikings and Falcons the Eagles advanced to Super Bowl XXXIX , where they dueled the New England Patriots .","entities":["NFC Championship","2004 season","Philadelphia Eagles","Westbrook","Terrell Owens","Falcons","McNabb","Super Bowl XXXIX","New England Patriots","Carolina Panthers","Vikings"],"facts":["NFC Championship -RELATED_TO-> Minneapolis Miracle","NFC Championship -PART_OF-> NFC","Nick Foles -PARTICIPATED_IN-> NFC Championship","TV Ratings: NFC Championship, American Idol, dominate weekly viewing -RELATED_TO-> NFC Championship","Minnesota Vikings -PARTICIPATED_IN-> NFC Championship"]}
