[E984209] {"title":"Firestone Tire and Rubber Company","text":"Firestone Tire and Rubber Company
The combined Bridgestone / Firestone North American operations are now based in Nashville , Tennessee . In 2008 , the companies celebrated a 20 - year anniversary of the merger , and changed the tire division name to Bridgestone Americas Tire Operations , LLC . In 2012 , Bridgestone Americas opened a $100 million technical center in Akron . Firestone tires used for the Indianapolis 500 race . Apart from tires , several companies and divisions operate with the Firestone brand in its name . These companies include Firestone Building Products , LLC , Firestone Industrial Products , LLC , Firestone Complete Auto Care , Firestone Natural Rubber Company and Firestone Specialty Products . Firestone Building Products and Firestone Industrial Products are headquartered in Indianapolis , Indiana and operate in 23 U.S. states and ten countries , with 11,000 employees worldwide . The company reports annual sales of more than $2.5 billion . In 1972 , Firestone received a ten - year import `` concession '' by the Kenyan government to secure Firestone 's investment in a domestic tire plant , which gave it a virtual monopoly . This included both general price and foreign exchange controls .","entities":["Firestone Complete Auto Care","Bridgestone / Firestone North American operations","Bridgestone Americas","Bridgestone Americas Tire Operations, LLC","technical center","Indianapolis 500 race","Firestone Building Products, LLC","Firestone Industrial Products, LLC","Firestone Specialty Products","Indianapolis","ten-year import concession","Kenyan government","domestic tire plant","20-year anniversary of the merger","Firestone Natural Rubber Company"],"facts":["Indianapolis -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Indianapolis team -LOCATED_IN-> Indianapolis","Opening of the first Firestone Complete Auto Care store -RELATED_TO-> Firestone Complete Auto Care","A Global Dream -RELATED_TO-> Bridgestone Americas","recruiter -LOCATED_IN-> Indianapolis"]}
[E8c5b96] {"title":"Firestone Tire and Rubber Company","text":"Firestone Tire and Rubber Company
Founded on August 3 , 1900 , the company initiated operations with 12 employees . Together , Firestone and Goodyear were the largest suppliers of automotive tires in North America for over 75 years . In 1906 Henry Ford chose Firestone for Model T original equipment tires . In 1918 , Firestone Tire and Rubber Company of Canada was incorporated in Hamilton , Ontario and in 1922 , the first Canadian - made tire rolled off the line on September 15 . During the 1920s , Firestone produced the Oldfield tire , named for racing driver Barney Oldfield . In 1926 , the company opened one of the world 's biggest rubber plantations in Liberia , West Africa , spanning more than 1 million acres . 1926 was also the year that the company opened its first Firestone Complete Auto Care store ( Firestone Complete Auto Care is a division of Firestone that offers automotive maintenance and repair ) . In 1927 , Henry Ford and tire maven Harvey Firestone took a trip to Los Angeles to select locations for their new factories .","entities":["Harvey Firestone","Goodyear","Henry Ford","Model T","Firestone Tire and Rubber Company of Canada","Hamilton","Oldfield tire","Barney Oldfield","Firestone Complete Auto Care","Incorporation of Firestone Tire and Rubber Company of Canada","First Canadian-made tire rolled off the line","Opening of Firestone's rubber plantation in Liberia","Opening of the first Firestone Complete Auto Care store","Trip to Los Angeles to select locations for new factories","Firestone Tire and Rubber Company"],"facts":["Goodyear -PART_OF-> Components companies","Goodyear -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Goodyear, Cavaliers Relationship Built on Shared Principles of Drive, Determination and Commitment to the Community","Goodyear -RELATED_TO-> IndyCar Series","Uncommon Friends: Life with Thomas Edison, Henry Ford, Harvey Firestone, Alexis Carrel, and Charles Lindbergh -RELATED_TO-> Harvey Firestone","Henry Ford -RELATED_TO-> Wilson"]}
