In Tom and Jerry : Spy Quest , they are seen working for Doctor Zin . They also make an appearance in Tom and Jerry : Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory . They were named after the Warner Bros. 1943 short Tin Pan Alley Cats . Tin is voiced by Greg Ellis , Pan by Jess Harnell and Alley by Richard McGonagle . Butch ( dog ) ( edit ) Main article : Butch Dog ( Tex Avery ) Butch ( Originally known as Spike , until renamed as Butch to avoid confusion with Spike from the Tom and Jerry cartoons ) is the name of another bulldog from Tex Avery 's shorts in the 1940s and 1950s . He was one of the main antagonists in Droopy shorts ( although he was replaced by Hanna - Barbera 's Spike in the 1980s ) and also had a series of his own . He appears in a number of movies e.g. Tom and Jerry and the Wizard of Oz and Tom and Jerry : The Magic Ring . References ( edit ) Jump up ^ Deitch , Gene ( 2015 ) .","entities":["Spike","Butch","Tom and Jerry: The Magic Ring","Jess Harnell","Tin","Pan","Alley","Tom and Jerry: Spy Quest","Doctor Zin","Tom and Jerry: Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory","Tin Pan Alley Cats","Greg Ellis","Richard McGonagle","Droopy shorts","Tom and Jerry cartoons"],"facts":["Spike -RELATED_TO-> Tom","Spike -RELATED_TO-> Dog Trouble","Spike -RELATED_TO-> Tyke","Spike -RELATED_TO-> Solid Serenade","Spike -RELATED_TO-> Jerry"]}
