Later Tom and Jerry shorts are set in what appears to be Mammy 's own house . Her face is never seen ( with the exception of 1950s Saturday Evening Puss , in which her face is very briefly seen as she runs towards the camera ) , and she usually wallops the cat ( whom she usually addresses as `` Thomas '' ) with a broom when he misbehaves . When Mammy was not present , other humans would sometimes be seen , usually from the neck down as well . Mammy would appear in many cartoons until 1952 's Push - Button Kitty ; Mammy 's character was retired after that year following McDaniel 's death . Later cartoons would instead show Tom and Jerry living with a 1950s suburban couple . Soon after , virtually all humans in the series had visible faces . Nibbles ( edit ) Main article : Nibbles ( Tom and Jerry ) Nibbles in the 1949 theatrical short The Little Orphan Nibbles ( also known as Tuffy ) is the little , blue / gray , diaper - wearing orphan mouse who is close to Jerry and appears frequently with him , especially in the comics .","entities":["Jerry","Tom","Saturday Evening Puss","Mammy","Push-Button Kitty","Tom and Jerry shorts","Mammy's own house","The Little Orphan","McDaniel's death","1950s suburban couple","Nibbles","McDaniel"],"facts":["Jerry -LOCATED_IN-> home","Jerry -RELATED_TO-> pet store","Jerry -RELATED_TO-> shark","Jerry -RELATED_TO-> Dog Trouble","Jerry -RELATED_TO-> Lightning"]}
