Platform number 11 is currently not in use and is trackless . Platform numbers 15 & 16 were part of the former Princes Bridge Station on the northern side of Platform number 14 , and were both demolished during the construction of Federation Square . Three concourses link the platforms . The main concourse is at the east end of the station , located off Swanston Street and the main dome , and has direct access to all platforms via escalators , stair and elevators . The Degraves Street subway runs under the centre of the station , exiting to Flinders Street at the north end , with stairs directly connecting to all platforms except for platform numbers 12 and 13 . The Elizabeth Street subway is at the west end , and has direct access via ramps to all platforms except for platform numbers 1 , 12 , 13 and 14 . Trains may use a different platform if the platform it is originally scheduled at is occupied .","entities":["Flinders Street railway station","Degraves Street subway","platform 1","Platform 11","Platform 15","Platform 16","Platform 14","Platform 12","Princes Bridge Station","Federation Square","Main concourse","Main dome","Elizabeth Street subway","Platform 13","Swanston Street"],"facts":["Flinders Street railway station -LOCATED_IN-> Queen Street","Flinders Street railway station -LOCATED_IN-> Victoria","Flinders Street railway station -LOCATED_IN-> Yarra River","Flinders Street railway station -LOCATED_IN-> Australia","Flinders Street railway station -LOCATED_IN-> Melbourne"]}
