He did not sign with the Royals . College career ( edit ) Sanders at Florida State Sanders enrolled at Florida State University and played three sports for the Florida State Seminoles : football , baseball , and track . Beginning his freshman year , he started in the Seminoles ' secondary , played outfield for the baseball team that finished fifth in the nation , and helped lead the track and field team to a conference championship . Under head coach Bobby Bowden , Sanders was a two - time consensus All - American cornerback in 1987 and 1988 , and a third team All - American in 1986 , intercepting 14 passes in his career , including three in bowl games , and managed to return one interception 100 yards for a touchdown breaking Fred Biletnikoff 's interception return record by one yard . He won the Jim Thorpe Award in 1988 . He was also a standout punt returner for Florida State , leading the nation in 1988 with his punt return average , and breaking the school 's record for career punt return yards .","entities":["baseball","track","football","Florida State Seminoles","Deion Sanders","Florida State University","Bobby Bowden","Jim Thorpe Award","Conference Championship","Fred Biletnikoff","All-American"],"facts":["baseball -RELATED_TO-> Houston","Game seven -RELATED_TO-> baseball","baseball -RELATED_TO-> Fayetteville, Houston Astros sign 30-year agreement to bring baseball to downtown","Dave Dravecky -RELATED_TO-> baseball","American League -RELATED_TO-> baseball"]}
