Emilio Scotto - wikipedia Emilio Scotto Jump to : navigation , search Emilio Scotto Emilio Walter Eduardo Alfredo SCOTTO ( 1954 - 09 - 27 ) September 27 , 1954 ( age 63 ) Buenos Aires , Argentina Residence Miami , Florida Nationality Argentine Occupation Motorcycle traveler , adventurer , writer and motivational speaker Spouse ( s ) Monica Pino Emilio Scotto ( Buenos Aires , September 27 , 1954 ) is an Argentine adventurer , photojournalist , and writer . As of 2009 he holds the Guinness record for the world 's longest motorcycle ride , spanning 10 years , 279 countries and a total distance of 457,000 miles ( 735,000 km ) . The ride was done on a 1980 Honda Gold Wing GL1100 motorcycle Scotto calls `` Black Princess . '' Scotto recounted his travels in a 224 - page book illustrated with his photographs , The Longest Ride : My Ten - Year 500,000 Mile Motorcycle Journey , published in 2007 .","entities":["Florida","Monica Pino","world's longest motorcycle ride","Honda Gold Wing GL1100","Guinness record for the world's longest motorcycle ride","Emilio Scotto","The Longest Ride: My Ten-Year 500,000 Mile Motorcycle Journey","Argentina","Miami","Buenos Aires"],"facts":["Florida -LOCATED_IN-> East Coast of the United States","Florida -LOCATED_IN-> U.S.","Florida -LOCATED_IN-> Self-defense","coral reefs -LOCATED_IN-> Florida","Florida -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
