[E684bfd] {"title":"Sentencing Reform Act","text":"Sentencing Reform Act
Sentencing Reform Act - Wikipedia Sentencing Reform Act Jump to : navigation , search The Sentencing Reform Act , part of the Comprehensive Crime Control Act of 1984 , was a U.S. federal statute intended to increase consistency in United States federal sentencing . It established the United States Sentencing Commission . It also abolished federal parole , except for persons convicted under federal law before November 1 , 1987 , persons convicted under District of Columbia law , `` transfer treaty '' inmates , persons who violated military law who are in federal civilian prisons , and persons who are defendants in state cases and who are under the U.S. Marshals Service Witness Protection Program . The act was passed by large majorities in both houses of Congress . References ( edit ) Jump up ^ `` An Overview of the United States Sentencing Commission '' ( PDF ) . United States Sentencing Commission . United States Sentencing Commission . Retrieved 9 August 2011 . Jump up ^ Barry L. Johnson . `` Sentencing Reform Act ( 1984 ) '' . eNotes . Retrieved 9 August 2011 .","entities":["United States","Congress","Comprehensive Crime Control Act of 1984","United States federal sentencing","United States Sentencing Commission","Federal parole","Military law","Witness Protection Program","An Overview of the United States Sentencing Commission","Barry L. Johnson","Sentencing Reform Act (1984)","Sentencing Reform Act","Federal law","U.S. Marshals Service","District of Columbia"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
