The initial plan was to have three five - team divisions per league with inter league play year - round -- possibly as many as 30 interleague games per team each year . For various reasons , it soon seemed more practical to have an even number of teams in both leagues . The Milwaukee Brewers agreed to change leagues , moving from the AL Central to the NL Central . At the same time , the Detroit Tigers were moved from the AL East to the AL Central , making room for the Devil Rays in the East . Following the move of the Houston Astros to the American League in 2013 , both leagues now consist of 15 teams . For the first 96 years , American League teams faced their National League counterparts only in exhibition games or in the World Series . Beginning in 1997 , interleague games have been played during the regular season and count in the standings . As part of the agreement instituting interleague play , the designated - hitter rule is used only in games where the American League team is the home team .","entities":["Detroit Tigers","World Series","Milwaukee Brewers","Devil Rays","interleague play","exhibition games","standings","designated-hitter rule","National League","AL East","AL Central","NL Central","Houston Astros","American League","Regular season"],"facts":["Detroit Tigers -LOCATED_IN-> Detroit","Detroit Tigers -PART_OF-> American League Central","Detroit Tigers -PART_OF-> American League Central","Detroit Tigers -PARTICIPATED_IN-> 1909 Game Seven","Detroit Tigers -PARTICIPATED_IN-> 1934 St. Louis Cardinals vs. Detroit Tigers"]}
