He felt that the characters , with the exception of Ivan Ooze , lacked personalities , and that the scenes of monsters rampaging through the city hearkened back to the worst Japanese monster films . Mick LaSalle of the San Francisco Chronicle found the fights `` only adequately choreographed , '' called the battle in the climax `` a complete disaster '' and stating that it made no sense in timing , that protagonists were not very intelligent , and the actors playing them unremarkable . Home media ( edit ) This section does not cite any sources . Please help improve this section by adding citations to reliable sources . Unsourced material may be challenged and removed . ( May 2015 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this template message ) The film was released on VHS and LaserDisc in late 1995 and then as a double feature with 1997 's Turbo : A Power Rangers Movie on a double - sided DVD in 2001 by 20th Century Fox Home Entertainment . Bonus features included a theatrical trailer and a `` Making Of '' featurette . The film was then released separately on a single - sided DVD in 2003 .","entities":["Ivan Ooze","Turbo: A Power Rangers Movie","20th Century Fox Home Entertainment","VHS","LaserDisc","DVD","theatrical trailer","Making Of","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie","Mick LaSalle","San Francisco Chronicle"],"facts":["Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie -LOCATED_IN-> Queensland","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie -LOCATED_IN-> California","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie -LOCATED_IN-> Sydney","Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie -RELATED_TO-> English"]}

