[Ee66d53] {"title":"FIFA World Rankings","text":"FIFA World Rankings
The teams of the member nations of FIFA , football 's world governing body , are ranked based on their game results with the most successful teams being ranked highest . The rankings were introduced in December 1992 , and eight teams ( Argentina , Belgium , Brazil , France , Germany , Italy , the Netherlands and Spain ) have held the top position , of which Brazil have spent longest ranked first . A points system is used , with points being awarded based on the results of all FIFA - recognised full international matches . Under the existing system , rankings are based on a team 's performance over the last four years , with more recent results and more significant matches being more heavily weighted to help reflect the current competitive state of a team . The ranking system was most recently revamped after the 2006 World Cup , with the first edition of the new series of rankings issued on 12 July 2006 . The most significant change is that the rankings are now based on results over the previous four years instead of the previous eight years .","entities":["the Netherlands","points system","FIFA-recognised full international matches","2006 World Cup","First edition of the new series of rankings","Brazil","Argentina","Belgium","FIFA World Rankings","FIFA","Italy","Spain","Germany","France"],"facts":["Brazil -RELATED_TO-> FIFA World Ranking","Brazil -RELATED_TO-> 2014 World Cup","2006 ranking system update -RELATED_TO-> 2006 World Cup","FIFA president Blatter a big loser with Germany getting 2006 World Cup -RELATED_TO-> 2006 World Cup","Brazil -RELATED_TO-> 2010 World Cup"]}
