Diselma , Fitzroya , Callitris ( incl . Actinostrobus and Neocallitropsis ) , Thujopsis , Thuja , Fokienia , Chamaecyparis , Callitropsis , Cupressus , Juniperus , Xanthocyparis , Calocedrus , Tetraclinis , Platycladus , Microbiota Family Taxaceae : Austrotaxus , Pseudotaxus , Taxus , Cephalotaxus , Amentotaxus , Torreya Diversity and origin ( edit ) There are more than 1000 extant or currently living species of gymnosperms in 88 plant genera belonging to 14 plant families . It is widely accepted that the gymnosperms originated in the late Carboniferous period , replacing the lycopsid rainforests of the tropical region . This appears to have been the result of a whole genome duplication event around 319 million years ago . Early characteristics of seed plants were evident in fossil progymnosperms of the late Devonian period around 383 million years ago .","entities":["Gymnosperm","Diselma","Fitzroya","Callitris","Actinostrobus","Neocallitropsis","Thujopsis","Thuja","Fokienia","Chamaecyparis","Callitropsis","Cupressus","Juniperus","Xanthocyparis","Calocedrus"],"facts":["Gymnosperm -RELATED_TO-> naked seeds","Gymnosperm -RELATED_TO-> varnish","Gymnosperm -RELATED_TO-> nail polish","Gymnosperm -RELATED_TO-> gum","Gymnosperm -RELATED_TO-> perfumes"]}
