Initially , its `` Settings '' dialog box was replaced by dedicated page in the Settings app . In Windows 10 Creators Update , Windows Defender is renamed Windows Defender Antivirus to distinguish it from Windows Defender Security Center . The latter has become the default avenue to interface with Windows Defender . While there is no shortcut on the Start menu for Windows Defender 's native client , it can still run . Advanced features ( edit ) Windows Defender successfully blocks the EICAR test file Real - time protection In the Windows Defender options , the user can configure real - time protection options . Browser integration Integration with Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge enables files to be scanned as they are downloaded to detect malicious software inadvertently downloaded . Although it does not integrate with non-Microsoft web browsers , Windows Defender scans for malicious downloaded files as part of its real - time protection . Windows 10 's Anniversary Update introduced Limited Periodic Scanning , which optionally allows Windows Defender to scan a system periodically if another antivirus app is installed . It also introduced Block at First Sight , which uses machine learning to predict whether a file is malicious . Windows Vista - specific functionality ( edit ) Windows Defender had additional functionality in Windows Vista which was removed in subsequent versions of Windows .","entities":["Microsoft Edge","Windows Defender","Windows Defender Security Center","Settings app","Windows 10 Creators Update","Windows 10 Anniversary Update","Limited Periodic Scanning","Block at First Sight","real-time protection","EICAR test file","Windows Vista","Windows Defender Settings dialog box","Start menu","antivirus app","Internet Explorer"],"facts":["Adobe Flash Player -RELATED_TO-> Microsoft Edge","Windows Defender -RELATED_TO-> Viruses","Windows Defender -RELATED_TO-> Windows XP","Windows Defender -RELATED_TO-> Windows 2000","Windows Defender -RELATED_TO-> Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License"]}
