Since Windows 10 Anniversary Update , offline functionality is integrated into the regular Windows Defender program . Mitigated Security vulnerability ( edit ) On 5 May 2017 , Tavis Ormandy , a vulnerability researcher for Google , discovered a security vulnerability in the JavaScript analysis module ( NScript ) of Microsoft Antimalware Engine ( MsMpEngine ) that impacted Windows Defender , Microsoft Security Essentials and System Center Endpoint Protection . By 8 May 2017 , Microsoft had released a patch to all affected systems . Ars Technica commended Microsoft for its unprecedented patching speed and said that the disaster had been averted . See also ( edit ) Security and safety features new to Windows Vista References ( edit ) Jump up ^ `` Windows Defender '' . Download Center . Microsoft . 23 May 2007 . Archived from the original on 29 April 2012 . ^ Jump up to : `` What is Windows Defender ? '' . Computer Hope . Retrieved 31 December 2017 . Jump up ^ Shultz , Greg . `` Windows Defender : Past , present , and future '' . Retrieved 13 June 2017 .","entities":["JavaScript","Google","Windows Defender","Microsoft Security Essentials","Windows 10 Anniversary Update","Windows Vista","Tavis Ormandy","Security vulnerability discovery","security vulnerability","NScript","Microsoft Antimalware Engine","System Center Endpoint Protection","Patch release","patch","Security and safety features new to Windows Vista"],"facts":["Google Swiffy -RELATED_TO-> JavaScript","Shumway -RELATED_TO-> JavaScript","Mozilla Shumway -RELATED_TO-> JavaScript","Toolkit for CreateJS -RELATED_TO-> JavaScript","ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> JavaScript"]}
