It occurs in mid-April each year , and coincides with the traditional new year in Assam , Bengal , Burma , Cambodia , Kerala , Kashmir , Manipur , Odisha , Punjab , Sri Lanka , Tamil Nadu and Thailand . In addition to Nepal , the Vikram Samvat calendar is also recognized in North and East India , and in Gujarat among Hindus . In Buddhist communities , the month of Baishakh is associated with Vesak or Buddha 's Birthday . It commemorates the birth , Enlightenment and passing of Gautama Buddha on the first full moon day in May , except in a leap year when the festival is held in June . Although this festival is not held on the same day as Pahela Baishakh , the holidays typically fall in the same month ( Baishakh ) of the Bengali , Hindu , and Theravada Buddhist calendars , and are related historically through the spread of Hinduism and Buddhism in South Asia . In Gujarat , the second day of Diwali is celebrated as the first day of the Vikram Samvat calendar which is the first day of the month Kartik .","entities":["Manipur","Tamil Nadu","Cambodia","Assam","Hinduism","Diwali","Buddhism","Hindus","Hindu calendar","Vikram Samvat","traditional new year","North and East India","Buddhist communities","Baishakh","Vesak"],"facts":["Article 371 -RELATED_TO-> Manipur","British wrested control of Manipur and Assam from the Burmese -RELATED_TO-> Manipur","Tamil Nadu -LOCATED_IN-> India","Coffee farms -LOCATED_IN-> Tamil Nadu","Eastern Coastal Plains -LOCATED_IN-> Tamil Nadu"]}
