Belgium ( edit ) In Belgium , the justice of the peace ( French : juge de paix , Dutch : vrederechter ) is a law - trained judge who sits the lowest Court of record with original jurisdiction over small claims ( less than € 2500 ) matters of civil , commercial , and family law , including : tenancy and lease disputes , neighborhood disputes ( party structures , trespassing , noise pollution ) , apartment buildings , small deceased estates , alimony , guardianships & adoption , and the commitment of mental patients and oversight of their care . Litigants may opt either for conciliation or trial . Lawyers may act as locum tenens JPs . Canada ( edit ) In Canada , justices of the peace play a role in the administration of justice at the provincial level . Justices are generally appointed by the lieutenant governors of Canada 's provinces , and by the commissioners of Canada 's territories , on the advice of their relevant premier or Attorney General .","entities":["Lieutenant governors","Belgium","Canada's provinces","Canada's territories","Commissioners","Premier","Attorney General","justice of the peace","Canada","Judge"],"facts":["Lieutenant governors -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag","Lieutenant governors -RELATED_TO-> Manitoba","Lieutenant governors -RELATED_TO-> Ontario","Lieutenant governors -RELATED_TO-> British Columbia","Lieutenant governors -LOCATED_IN-> India"]}
