( PLD 2016 Supreme Court 581 ) It is pertinent to note however , as many academics have pointed out , that there is great utility in the appointment of such justices especially in rural areas where enmity between rival groups can lead to the inability of registration of cognizable offences and biased judicial proceedings . Singapore ( edit ) A justice of the peace in Singapore derives his powers from statute law . He is appointed by the President of the Republic of Singapore , under the provisions of section 11 ( l ) of the Subordinate Courts Act ( Cap. 321 ) . The President may revoke the appointment of any justice of the peace . A newly appointed justice of the peace is required by section 17 of the Subordinate Courts Act , to take the oath of office and allegiance as set out in the schedule to the Subordinate Courts Act , before exercising the functions of his office . In their role , JPs serve as visiting justices of Singapore prisons , mediators or referees in the subordinate courts . They may also solemnise marriages in the Registry of Marriages or perform the duties of the magistrate conferred on them by any written law .","entities":["Singapore","President of the Republic of Singapore","statute law","Subordinate Courts Act","Singapore prisons","subordinate courts","Registry of Marriages","oath of office and allegiance","mediator","referee","magistrate","justice of the peace"],"facts":["Singapore -LOCATED_IN-> Singapore Bar Examination (Part B)","Singapore -LOCATED_IN-> Asia","Singapore stock exchange -LOCATED_IN-> Singapore","Pathlight School -LOCATED_IN-> Singapore","Singapore -LOCATED_IN-> Pretoria"]}
