Twelve - step program - wikipedia Twelve - step program Jump to : navigation , search A twelve - step program is a set of guiding principles outlining a course of action for recovery from addiction , compulsion , or other behavioral problems . Originally proposed by Alcoholics Anonymous ( AA ) as a method of recovery from alcoholism , the Twelve Steps were first published in the 1939 book Alcoholics Anonymous : The Story of How More Than One Hundred Men Have Recovered from Alcoholism . The method was adapted and became the foundation of other twelve - step programs . As summarized by the American Psychological Association , the process involves the following : admitting that one can not control one 's alcoholism , addiction or compulsion ; recognizing a higher power that can give strength ; examining past errors with the help of a sponsor ( experienced member ) ; making amends for these errors ; learning to live a new life with a new code of behavior ; helping others who suffer from the same alcoholism , addictions or compulsions .","entities":["alcoholism","Alcoholics Anonymous: The Story of How More Than One Hundred Men Have Recovered from Alcoholism","other twelve-step programs","higher power","sponsor","new code of behavior","Alcoholics Anonymous","Compulsion","Twelve Steps","Twelve-step program","American Psychological Association","Addiction","behavioral problems"],"facts":["alcoholism -RELATED_TO-> Alcohol","alcoholism -RELATED_TO-> malnutrition","World Health Organization -RELATED_TO-> alcoholism","Alcohol -RELATED_TO-> alcoholism","alcoholism -RELATED_TO-> life expectancy"]}
[E4acd27] {"title":"Twelve-step program","text":"Twelve-step program
Contents ( hide ) 1 Overview 2 History 3 Twelve Steps 4 Twelve Traditions 5 Process 6 Sponsorship 7 Effectiveness 8 Criticism 8.1 Confidentiality 8.2 Cultural identity 9 See also 10 References 11 Further reading 11.1 Scholarly publications Overview ( edit ) Twelve - step methods have been adapted to address a wide range of alcoholism , substance - abuse and dependency problems . Over 200 self - help organizations -- often known as fellowships -- with a worldwide membership of millions -- now employ twelve - step principles for recovery . Narcotics Anonymous was formed by addicts who did not relate to the specifics of alcohol dependency . Demographic preferences related to the addicts ' drug of choice has led to the creation of Cocaine Anonymous , Crystal Meth Anonymous and Marijuana Anonymous . Behavioral issues such as compulsion for , and / or addiction to , gambling , crime , food , sex , hoarding , debting and work are addressed in fellowships such as Gamblers Anonymous , Overeaters Anonymous , Sexaholics Anonymous and Debtors Anonymous .","entities":["Crime","alcoholism","gambling","Twelve-step methods","Dependency","Self-help organizations","Narcotics Anonymous","Addicts","Alcohol dependency","Demographic preferences","Drug of choice","Cocaine Anonymous","Crystal Meth Anonymous","Marijuana Anonymous","Behavioral issues"],"facts":["Begar -RELATED_TO-> Crime","Attempted suicide -RELATED_TO-> Crime","Article 21 -RELATED_TO-> Crime","2016 White House report -RELATED_TO-> Crime","study by the Council of Economic Advisers -RELATED_TO-> Crime"]}
