Engineering ( edit ) Post and lintel construction is one of four ancient structural methods of building , the others being the corbel , arch - and - vault , and truss . There are two main force vectors acting upon the post and lintel system : weight carrying compression at the joint between lintel and post , and tension induced by deformation of self - weight and the load above between the posts . The two posts are under compression from the weight of the lintel ( or beam ) above . The lintel will deform by sagging in the middle because the underside is under tension and the topside is under compression . See also ( edit ) Wikimedia Commons has media related to Post and Beam and Lintels .","entities":["Wikimedia Commons","post","Ancient structural methods of building","Corbel","Arch-and-vault","Truss","Compression","Joint","Deformation","Post and Beam and Lintels","Lintel","Post and lintel","tension"],"facts":["Wikimedia Commons -RELATED_TO-> Alice in Wonderland (1951 film)","Wikimedia Commons -RELATED_TO-> Cyrus Cylinder","Wikimedia Commons -RELATED_TO-> Governors-General of India","Wikimedia Commons -RELATED_TO-> Reading F.C.","Wikimedia Commons -RELATED_TO-> Nobel Prize in Physics"]}
