The pattern of flow is organized by the rotation of the Earth and the presence of the solid inner core . The mechanism by which the Earth generates a magnetic field is known as a dynamo . The magnetic field is generated by a feedback loop : current loops generate magnetic fields ( Ampère 's circuital law ) ; a changing magnetic field generates an electric field ( Faraday 's law ) ; and the electric and magnetic fields exert a force on the charges that are flowing in currents ( the Lorentz force ) .","entities":["solid inner core","rotation of the Earth","feedback loop","current loops","Ampère's circuital law","electric field","Faraday's law","Lorentz force","charges","magnetic field","dynamo","currents","Earth"],"facts":["magnetic field -RELATED_TO-> vector field","solid inner core -PART_OF-> Earth's core","solid inner core -RELATED_TO-> heat flow","charges -RELATED_TO-> speeding","magnetic field -RELATED_TO-> Cartesian components"]}
