This may have evolved to carry out the reverse reaction and act as an ATP synthase . In different species ( edit ) E coli ( edit ) E. coli ATP synthase is the simplest known form of ATP synthase , with 8 different subunit types . Yeast ( edit ) Yeast ATP synthase is one of the best - studied eukaryotic ATP synthases ; and five F , eight F subunits , and seven associated proteins have been identified . Most of these proteins have homologues in other eukaryotes . Plant ( edit ) In plants , ATP synthase is also present in chloroplasts ( CF F - ATP synthase ) . The enzyme is integrated into thylakoid membrane ; the CF - part sticks into stroma , where dark reactions of photosynthesis ( also called the light - independent reactions or the Calvin cycle ) and ATP synthesis take place . The overall structure and the catalytic mechanism of the chloroplast ATP synthase are almost the same as those of the mitochondrial enzyme . However , in chloroplasts , the proton motive force is generated not by respiratory electron transport chain but by primary photosynthetic proteins .","entities":["ATP synthase","thylakoid membrane","proton motive force","E. coli ATP synthase","E. coli","Yeast ATP synthase","Yeast","chloroplast ATP synthase","chloroplasts","CF-part","stroma","dark reactions","mitochondrial enzyme","respiratory electron transport chain","primary photosynthetic proteins"],"facts":["ATP synthase -RELATED_TO-> electrochemical gradient","ATP synthase -RELATED_TO-> proton gradient","ATP synthase -RELATED_TO-> bovine heart mitochondria","ATP synthase -RELATED_TO-> Partial resolution of the enzymes catalyzing oxidative phosphorylation. 8. Properties of a factor conferring oligomycin sensitivity on mitochondrial adenosine triphosphatase","ATP synthase -RELATED_TO-> H"]}
