Philippe Petit - wikipedia Philippe Petit Jump to : navigation , search Philippe Petit Petit at the 81st Academy Awards in February 2009 ( 1949 - 08 - 13 ) 13 August 1949 ( age 68 ) Nemours , Seine - et - Marne , France Occupation High - wire artist Philippe Petit ( French pronunciation : ​ ( filip pəti ) ; born 13 August 1949 ) is a French high - wire artist who gained fame for his high - wire walk between the Twin Towers of the World Trade Center in New York City , on the morning of August 7 , 1974 as well as his high wire walk between the Notre Dame cathedral in Paris , 1971 . For his unauthorized feat 400 metres ( 1,000 feet ) above the ground -- which he referred to as `` le coup '' -- he rigged a 200 - kilogram ( 440 - pound ) cable and used a custom - made 8 - metre ( 30 - foot ) long , 25 - kilogram ( 55 - pound ) balancing pole . He performed for 45 minutes , making eight passes along the wire .","entities":["New York City","France","World Trade Center","Nemours","Seine-et-Marne","High-wire walk between the Twin Towers","Twin Towers","High-wire walk between Notre Dame cathedral and Paris","Notre Dame cathedral","Philippe Petit","Paris"],"facts":["New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New Jersey","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York (state)","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> North America","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
