INF Treaty Post-Presidency Presidential Library Medal of Freedom Bibliography An American Life The Reagan Diaries Alzheimer 's diagnosis State funeral Legacy Speeches and debates `` A Time for Choosing '' Reagan Era Reagan Award `` A Time for Choosing '' , also known as `` The Speech '' , was a speech presented during the 1964 U.S. presidential election campaign by future president Ronald Reagan on behalf of Republican candidate Barry Goldwater . The speech launched Reagan into national prominence . Contents ( hide ) 1 Background 2 Aftermath 3 References 4 Further reading 5 External links Background ( edit ) Many versions of the speech exist , since it was altered over many weeks . Contrary to popular belief , however , the speech was not given at the 1964 Republican National Convention in San Francisco , California as a nomination speech for presidential candidate Senator Barry Goldwater ; Richard Nixon gave that nomination speech . Reagan , though he campaigned for Goldwater , did not use `` A Time for Choosing '' until October 27 , 1964 , when it was part of a pre-recorded television program , Rendezvous with Destiny .","entities":["San Francisco","Richard Nixon","A Time for Choosing","1964 U.S. presidential election campaign","Rendezvous with Destiny","1964 Republican National Convention","Barry Goldwater","Ronald Reagan","California"],"facts":["San Francisco -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Asian Art Museum -LOCATED_IN-> San Francisco","AT&T Park -LOCATED_IN-> San Francisco","1990 San Francisco performance of The Sleeping Beauty -LOCATED_IN-> San Francisco","Candlestick Park -LOCATED_IN-> San Francisco"]}
