Locations included Burbank , Downey , New York City , LA / Ontario International Airport ( which doubled for Miami International Airport ) , Quebec City and Montreal . The film was shot in 147 locations in only 52 days . DiCaprio reflected , `` Scenes that we thought would take three days took an afternoon '' . Filming ran from April 25 -- 30 in Park Avenue , just outside the Waldorf - Astoria Hotel . Production moved to Orange , New Jersey and returned to Brooklyn for bank and courthouse scenes . Shooting also took place at the TWA Flight Center at John F. Kennedy International Airport . Quebec City was chosen for its European character and French feel . Place Royale , within Old Quebec , stands for Montrichard -- the church in the background of the arrest scene is Notre - Dame - des - Victoires . Filming ended on May 12 in Montreal . Music ( edit ) Main article : Catch Me If You Can ( soundtrack ) The film 's soundtrack was released on December 10 , 2002 by DreamWorks Records . The original score was composed and conducted by John Williams .","entities":["New York City","Montreal","Brooklyn","Miami International Airport","Montrichard","Downey","Ontario International Airport","Park Avenue","Orange, New Jersey","TWA Flight Center","John F. Kennedy International Airport","Place Royale","Old Quebec","Notre-Dame-des-Victoires","Filming in Park Avenue"],"facts":["New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New Jersey","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> New York (state)","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> North America","New York City -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
