[Ec0bed8] {"title":"Catch Me If You Can","text":"Catch Me If You Can
The film is based on the life of Frank Abagnale , who , before his 19th birthday , successfully performed cons worth millions of dollars by posing as a Pan American World Airways pilot , a Georgia doctor and a Louisiana parish prosecutor . His primary crime was check fraud ; he became so experienced that the FBI eventually turned to him for help in catching other checking forgers . The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio and Tom Hanks , with Christopher Walken , Martin Sheen , and Nathalie Baye in supporting roles . Development for the film started in 1980 , but did not progress until 1997 , when the film rights to Abagnale 's book were sold to Spielberg 's DreamWorks . David Fincher , Gore Verbinski , Lasse Hallström , Miloš Forman , and Cameron Crowe had all been possible candidates for director before Spielberg decided to direct . Filming took place from February to May 2002 . The film was a financial and critical success , and was received positively by both critics and Abagnale .","entities":["Filming","Louisiana","Frank Abagnale","Pan American World Airways","DreamWorks","Lasse Hallström","Abagnale's book","check fraud","Film development","Film rights sale","FBI","Tom Hanks","Nathalie Baye","Martin Sheen","David Fincher"],"facts":["Filming -LOCATED_IN-> Vancouver","Filming -LOCATED_IN-> United States Penitentiary, Atlanta","Filming -LOCATED_IN-> Amity Compound","Filming -LOCATED_IN-> Peachtree Center","Filming -LOCATED_IN-> Hatley Castle"]}

