Konami , the first third - party company that was allowed to make cartridges for the Famicom , would later circumvent this rule by creating a spinoff company , Ultra Games , to release additional games in a single year . Other manufacturers soon employed the same tactic . Also in 1985 , Super Mario Bros. was released for the Famicom in Japan and became a large success . Nintendo test marketed the Nintendo Entertainment System in the New York area on October 18 , 1985 . They expanded the test to Los Angeles in February 1986 , followed by tests in Chicago and San Francisco . They would go national by the end of 1986 , along with 15 games , sold separately . In the US and Canada , it outsold its competitors by a wide margin . This was also the year that Metroid and Super Mario Bros. 2 ( the Japanese version ) were released . In 1987 , The Legend of Zelda was released to much critical acclaim . In 1988 , Nintendo of America unveiled Nintendo Power , a monthly news and strategy magazine from Nintendo that served to advertise new games .","entities":["US","Los Angeles","San Francisco","Famicom","Konami","Ultra Games","Super Mario Bros.","Nintendo Entertainment System","New York area","Nintendo Power","Super Mario Bros. 2","Nintendo of America","Nintendo","Metroid","Japan"],"facts":["Washington DC -LOCATED_IN-> US","Missouri -LOCATED_IN-> US","Pennsylvania -LOCATED_IN-> US","US speed limit decrease -LOCATED_IN-> US","US -LOCATED_IN-> Edison Tech Center"]}
