Approximately half the colonists of European ancestry tried to avoid involvement in the struggle -- some of them deliberate pacifists , others recent immigrants , and many more simple apolitical folk . The patriots received active support from perhaps 40 to 45 percent of the white populace , and at most no more than a bare majority . A jury finding from Kentucky County , Virginia in July 1780 , confiscating lands of two men adjudged to be British subject . Daniel Boone was listed as a member of the jury . Before Calhoon 's work , estimates of the Loyalist share of the population were somewhat higher , at about one - third , but these estimates are now rejected as too high by most scholars . In 1968 historian Paul H. Smith estimated there were about 400,000 Loyalists , or 16 % of the white population of 2.25 million in 1780 .","entities":["Patriots","Daniel Boone","Virginia","jury","jury finding","Kentucky County","British subject","American Revolution","Loyalist","Paul H. Smith"],"facts":["Patriots -LOCATED_IN-> South Carolina","Patriots -RELATED_TO-> Pittsburgh Steelers","Patriots -RELATED_TO-> Dallas Cowboys","Patriots -RELATED_TO-> Indianapolis Colts","Patriots -LOCATED_IN-> Boston"]}
