Bush and who had been a lawyer in James Baker 's firm , Baker Botts . The SEC 's general counsel at the time was James Doty , who had been appointed by President H.W. Bush and as a lawyer in James Baker 's firm , Baker Botts had represented George W. Bush when arrangements were made to acquire the Texas Rangers baseball franchise ( although Doty recused himself from the investigation . ) . With Baker Botts representing W. Bush , the Saudi BinLaden family and W. Bush 's funding conduit James R. Bath , Doty was involved in the frivilous litigation campaign launched in the attempt to intimidate BinLaden middleman James R Bath 's business partner ( ( Charles W. ( `` Bill '' ) White ) ) into cooperating with the attempted cover - up of secret BinLaden Family funding of W. Bush 's campaigns and businesses . Bush 's own lawyer was Robert Jordan , who had been `` partners with both Doty and Breeden at Baker Botts and who later became George W. Bush 's ambassador to Saudi Arabia '' .","entities":["Saudi Arabia","SEC","James Baker","Baker Botts","James Doty","H.W. Bush","Texas Rangers baseball franchise","Saudi BinLaden family","James R. Bath","frivolous litigation campaign","Charles W. White","Robert Jordan","Breeden","attempted cover-up of secret BinLaden Family funding of W. Bush's campaigns and businesses","George W. Bush"],"facts":["Saudi Arabia -LOCATED_IN-> Asia","Saudi Aramco -LOCATED_IN-> Saudi Arabia","Riyadh -LOCATED_IN-> Saudi Arabia","Australians in Saudi Arabia -LOCATED_IN-> Saudi Arabia","Saudi Arabia -LOCATED_IN-> Middle East"]}
