Examples are western ballet and modern dance , Classical Indian dance and Chinese and Japanese song and dance dramas . Most classical forms are centred upon dance alone , but performance dance may also appear in opera and other forms of musical theatre . Participatory dance , on the other hand , whether it be a folk dance , a social dance , a group dance such as a line , circle , chain or square dance , or a partner dance such as is common in western Western ballroom dancing , is undertaken primarily for a common purpose , such as social interaction or exercise , of participants rather than onlookers . Such dance seldom has any narrative . A group dance and a corps de ballet , a social partner dance and a pas de deux , differ profoundly . Even a solo dance may be undertaken solely for the satisfaction of the dancer . Participatory dancers often all employ the same movements and steps but , for example , in the rave culture of electronic dance music , vast crowds may engage in free dance , uncoordinated with those around them . On the other hand , some cultures lay down strict rules as to the particular dances in which , for example , men , women and children may or must participate .","entities":["cultures","western ballet","Classical Indian dance","Chinese and Japanese song and dance dramas","performance dance","musical theatre","participatory dance","folk dance","social dance","group dance","line dance","circle dance","chain dance","partner dance","western ballroom dancing"],"facts":["folk dance -RELATED_TO-> Estonia","Public holidays -RELATED_TO-> cultures","I/O psychologist -RELATED_TO-> cultures","cultures -RELATED_TO-> U.S. demographics","folk dance -RELATED_TO-> immigrant communities"]}
