Apostles ' Creed - wikipedia Apostles ' Creed Jump to : navigation , search The rubric above this 13th - century illuminated manuscript translates `` twelve articles of faith set out by twelve apostles '' . The Apostles ' Creed ( Latin : Symbolum Apostolorum or Symbolum Apostolicum ) , sometimes entitled Symbol of the Apostles , is an early statement of Christian belief -- a creed or `` symbol '' . It is widely used by a number of Christian denominations for both liturgical and catechetical purposes , most visibly by liturgical Churches of Western tradition , including the Catholic Church , Lutheranism and Anglicanism . It is also used by Presbyterians , Methodists and Congregationalists . The Apostles ' Creed is Trinitarian in structure with sections affirming belief in God the Father , Jesus Christ His Son and the Holy Spirit . The Apostles ' Creed was based on Christian theological understanding of the Canonical gospels , the letters of the New Testament and to a lesser extent the Old Testament . Its basis appears to be the old Roman Creed known also as the Old Roman Symbol .","entities":["Anglicanism","Lutheranism","Catholic Church","Congregationalists","Methodists","Old Testament","Apostles' Creed","Liturgical Churches of Western tradition","Christian belief","God the Father","Christian theological understanding","Canonical gospels","Letters of the New Testament","Old Roman Creed","Liturgical purposes"],"facts":["Catholic Church -RELATED_TO-> homosexuality","Church Fathers -RELATED_TO-> Lutheranism","Church Fathers -RELATED_TO-> Anglicanism","Catholic Church -RELATED_TO-> Tax on hops","Catholic Church -RELATED_TO-> kissing between males"]}
