28 -- 30 minutes . Specials Production company ( s ) BBC Scotland Distributor BBC Release Original network CBeebies Picture format 16 : 9 Widescreen Audio format Stereo Original release 10 February 2002 -- 14 April 2005 External links Website www.bbc.co.uk/cbeebies/shows/balamory Balamory is a Scottish live action television series on British television ( BBC One , BBC Two and CBeebies ) for pre school children , about a fictional small island community called Balamory in Scotland . It was produced between 10 February 2002 and 14 April 2005 by BBC Scotland , with 254 episodes made ( including a DVD exclusive Christmas episode ) . The series was created by Brian Jameson . Balamory was filmed mostly in Tobermory on the Isle of Mull , with the exception of scenes at Archie 's castle filmed at Fenton Tower in North Berwick , and other scenes , such as Camden and the nursery filmed in Glasgow . A select series of episodes was shown for two brief seasons in the United States on the Discovery Kids channel . It was also shown on TLC .","entities":["United States","Scotland","TLC","Glasgow","BBC","BBC One","Balamory","Brian Jameson","BBC Scotland","CBeebies","Discovery Kids","Tobermory","Isle of Mull","Fenton Tower","North Berwick"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
