Fore ( golf ) - Wikipedia Fore ( golf ) Jump to : navigation , search The tough rubber core of a golf ball makes it a hazard to others following a wayward shot , despite its weight not exceeding 45.93 g ( 1.62 oz ) `` Fore ! '' , originally an Australian interjection , is used to warn anyone standing or moving in the flight of a golf ball . The mention of the term in an 1881 Australian Golf Museum indicates that the term was in use at least as early as that period . It is believed to come from the military `` beware before '' , which an artilleryman about to fire would yell alerting nearby infantrymen to drop to the ground to avoid the shells overhead . ( Before may mean `` in front of ( the gun being fired ) '' ; fore may mean `` ( look ) ahead '' . ) Other possible origins include the term being derived from the term `` fore - caddie '' , a caddie waiting down range from the golfer to find where the ball lands .","entities":["Fore!","golf ball","Australian Golf Museum","beware before","fore-caddie"],"facts":["fore-caddie -RELATED_TO-> Fore","Fore! -RELATED_TO-> golf ball","Fore! -RELATED_TO-> Australian Golf Museum","Fore! -RELATED_TO-> beware before","Fore! -RELATED_TO-> fore-caddie"]}
[E60112b] {"title":"Fore (golf)","text":"Fore (golf)
These caddies were often warned about oncoming golf balls by a shout of the term `` fore - caddie '' which was eventually shortened to just `` fore ! '' . The Colonel Bogey March is based on the descending minor third which the original Colonel Bogey whistled instead of yelling Fore around 1914 . Notes ( edit ) Jump up ^ SND : Fore ^ Jump up to : Why Do Golfers Yell `` Fore '' for Errant Shots ? retrieved June 15 , 2007 Jump up ^ Derivation 4 Fore ! and Caddie retrieved June 15 , 2007 Jump up ^ The Windsor Magazine : An Illustrated Monthly for Men and Women Vol. 33 , no . 192 ( December 1910 ) References ( edit ) Scott , James Sibbald David , The British Army : Its Origin , Progress , and Equipment , 1868 Windsor Magazine : An Illustrated Monthly for Men and Women Vol. 32 , no . 292 ( December 1910 ) This golf - related article is a stub . You can help Wikipedia by expanding it .","entities":["Golf","fore-caddie","Fore","The Colonel Bogey March","descending minor third","Colonel Bogey","Why Do Golfers Yell “Fore” for Errant Shots?","Derivation 4 Fore! and Caddie","The Windsor Magazine: An Illustrated Monthly for Men and Women","Scott, James Sibbald David","The British Army: Its Origin, Progress, and Equipment","The British Army"],"facts":["HouseGuests -RELATED_TO-> Golf","Gerald Ford -RELATED_TO-> Golf","NBC Sports -RELATED_TO-> Golf","Golf -PART_OF-> Sport","Fore! -RELATED_TO-> fore-caddie"]}
