That year his biological father , whom Ford described as a `` carefree , well - to - do man who did n't really give a damn about the hopes and dreams of his firstborn son '' , approached Ford while he was waiting tables in a Grand Rapids restaurant . The two `` maintained a sporadic contact '' until Leslie King , Sr. 's death in 1941 . Ford said , `` My stepfather was a magnificent person and my mother equally wonderful . So I could n't have written a better prescription for a superb family upbringing . '' Eagle Scout Gerald Ford ( circled in red ) in 1929 ; Michigan Governor Fred W. Green at far left , holding hat Ford as a center on the University of Michigan football team , 1933 Ford was involved in the Boy Scouts of America , and earned that program 's highest rank , Eagle Scout . He is the only Eagle Scout to have ascended to the U.S. Presidency . Ford attended Grand Rapids South High School , where he was a star athlete and captain of the football team . In 1930 , he was selected to the All - City team of the Grand Rapids City League .","entities":["Boy Scouts of America","University of Michigan","Leslie King, Sr.","Fred W. Green","Eagle Scout","U.S. Presidency","Grand Rapids South High School","University of Michigan football team","All-City team","Grand Rapids City League","Selection to the All-City team","Grand Rapids","Gerald Ford"],"facts":["founding of the Boy Scouts of America -RELATED_TO-> Boy Scouts of America","Eagle Scout Welcome Gerald Ford Home -RELATED_TO-> Boy Scouts of America","President of the United States -RELATED_TO-> Boy Scouts of America","President Ford Field Service Council -PART_OF-> Boy Scouts of America","Boy Scouts of America -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Boy Scouts of America desegregates on the basis of race"]}
