Legal jurisdiction As per operations jurisdiction Governing body California State Legislature Constituting instrument Senate Bill 869 Headquarters Sacramento , California Officers 7,608 ( as of 2016 ) Civilians 3,276 ( as of 2014 ) Commissioner responsible Warren Stanley Parent agency California State Transportation Agency ( CALSTA ) Facilities Commands 8 Field Divisions 16 Commercial Enforcement Facilities 103 Area Offices Patrol cars Ford Explorer - based Police Interceptor Utility Vehicle Dodge Charger - Police Ford Crown Victoria - Police Planes Cessna 206 Website http://www.chp.ca.gov http://www.chpcareers.com The California Highway Patrol ( CHP ) is a law enforcement agency of the state of California . The primary mission of the CHP is to ensure safety and enforce traffic laws on all California highways and county roads in unincorporated areas . The CHP promotes traffic safety by inspecting commercial vehicles , as well as inspecting and certifying school buses , ambulances , and other specialized vehicles . The California State Legislature established the California Highway Patrol as a branch of the Division of Motor Vehicles in the Department of Public Works , with legislation signed by Governor C. C. Young on August 14 , 1929 .","entities":["California","California State Transportation Agency","California State Legislature","Division of Motor Vehicles","Department of Public Works","C. C. Young","Senate Bill 869","Signing of legislation establishing the California Highway Patrol","Sacramento","Warren Stanley","California Highway Patrol"],"facts":["California -LOCATED_IN-> United States","California -LOCATED_IN-> US","California -LOCATED_IN-> United States of America","California -LOCATED_IN-> California's rules governing professional attorney conduct","California -LOCATED_IN-> Missouri"]}
