This led to a cascade of effects whereby successful tenant farmers became agrarian capitalists ; unsuccessful ones became wage - labourers , required to sell their labour in order to live ; and landlords promoted the privatisation and renting out of common land , not least through the enclosures . In this reading , ' it was not merchants or manufacturers who drove the process that propelled the early development of capitalism . The transformation of social property relations was firmly rooted in the countryside , and the transformation of England 's trade and industry was result more than cause of England 's transition to capitalism ' . The present article includes both perspectives . Twenty - first - century developments ( edit ) The twenty - first century has seen renewed interest in the history of capitalism , and `` History of Capitalism '' has become a field in its own right , with courses in history departments . In the 2000s , Harvard University founded the Program on the Study of U.S. Capitalism ; Cornell University established the History of Capitalism Initiative ; and Columbia University Press launched a monograph series entitled Studies in the History of U.S. Capitalism .","entities":["Harvard University","England","Cornell University","Columbia University Press","Capitalism","Program on the Study of U.S. Capitalism","History of Capitalism Initiative","Studies in the History of U.S. Capitalism","History of capitalism"],"facts":["Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Liberia","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Sierra Leone","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Harvard update on West Africa Ebola outbreak: October 2014","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Early Mesopotamian Urbanism: A new view from the North","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Guinea"]}
