[E4ef808] {"title":"Dubai World Trade Centre","text":"Dubai World Trade Centre
Renamed after the late Sheikh Rashid Bin Saeed Al Maktoum , the 39 - storey Sheikh Rashid Tower no longer stands alone as it did when it was first built . Over the years , the Dubai World Trade Centre has been extended to include Exhibition Halls , Sheikh Rashid Hall and Maktoum Hall as well as the Al Mulaqua Ballroom , Sheikh Saeed Halls , Za'abeel Halls and the Trade Centre Arena . In addition , commercial buildings have been added including the Convention Tower and the One Central development with several mixed - use buildings . Dubai World Trade Centre today ( edit ) Dubai World Trade Centre has grown and added several business divisions to its overall portfolio . External links ( edit ) Official website Records First None recognized before Tallest building in Dubai 1979 -- 1999 Succeeded by Emirates Office Tower Landmarks and attractions in Dubai Al Bastakiya Al Fahidi Fort Atlantis ,","entities":["Atlantis","Dubai World Trade Centre","Sheikh Rashid Tower","Sheikh Rashid Bin Saeed Al Maktoum","Exhibition Halls","Sheikh Rashid Hall","Maktoum Hall","Al Mulaqua Ballroom","Sheikh Saeed Halls","Za'abeel Halls","Trade Centre Arena","Convention Tower","One Central","Dubai","Emirates Office Tower"],"facts":["The Behemoth -RELATED_TO-> Atlantis","Dubai -LOCATED_IN-> United Arab Emirates","Dubai World Trade Centre -RELATED_TO-> 100 dirham bank note","Dubai World Trade Centre -RELATED_TO-> trade events held at Dubai World Trade Centre","Dubai -LOCATED_IN-> UAE"]}
