[Eb02772] {"title":"Jack McCoy","text":"Jack McCoy
By the end of the 18th season , however , McCoy discovers that Shalvoy is involved in a prostitution scandal that is tied to a murder case he is prosecuting . Angered and disappointed , McCoy orders Cutter to start investigating Shalvoy , who retaliates by lending his support to McCoy 's opponent in the election . In the last episode of season 19 , `` The Drowned and the Saved '' , Cutter uncovers evidence that Shalvoy tried to buy a Senate seat for his wife , and threatens him with public disgrace unless he resigns . McCoy 's opponent suddenly has no patron , giving McCoy good prospects for victory . In the opening episode of season 20 , McCoy was revealed to have won the election ; he serves as DA for the remainder of this final season of Law & Order . Personal Life ( edit ) While he is a brilliant legal mind , McCoy has more than a few personal demons . He was abused by his father , an Irish Chicago policeman who had also beat Jack 's mother , and who eventually died of cancer . McCoy says that his determination and unyielding work ethic are a byproduct of having been harshly punished by his father for losing at anything .","entities":["cancer","the election","Chicago","Shalvoy","Cutter","McCoy's opponent","Shalvoy's wife","Jack McCoy's father","Jack McCoy's mother","prostitution scandal","murder case","Senate seat","The Drowned and the Saved","Law & Order","Jack McCoy"],"facts":["cancer -RELATED_TO-> postmenopausal women","Comeback -RELATED_TO-> cancer","When You Can't Come Back -RELATED_TO-> cancer","Dave Dravecky -RELATED_TO-> cancer","cancer -RELATED_TO-> Dave Dravecky"]}
